rtages + warehouses) and a Submit button, deployed on Vercel via GitHub.\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n### Critical User Decisions & Quotes:\n- **API Limits & Provider Pivot**: The user was frustrated by Google Gemini's 20 requests/day limit. They provided an OpenRouter API key (`[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]`) and instructed the agent to use free models via `openrouter/free`.\n- **Execution Speed**: The LLM batch processing took ~30 minutes for 1000 items, which the user found unacceptable for a web application. \"أنا عارف إن الـ requests كتيرة اه، بس يعني أكيد في حل يعني. عايز أحل مشكلتي اللي هو بيطول أوي عشان ألاقي response.\"\n- **Approval of Hybrid Architecture**: The user approved the Agent's proposal to use a local Vector/TF-IDF filter before the LLM step, but with a strict instruction: \"تمام نفذ فكرتك في فولدر جوا المشروع يبقي منفصل وقولي هنفضل نستخدم الapi بتاع unstructed.io ولا خلاص كدا\".\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n### Codebase Hardening & API Migrations:\n- **OpenRouter Integration**: Stripped the Google GenAI SDK and successfully migrated the matching pipeline to OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible REST API. \n- **Prompt & Parsing Resilience**: Discovered that generic open-source models (routed via `openrouter/free`) fail to understand highly compressed JSON keys (e.g., `{\"s\": \"m\"}`) and fail if forced into `json_object` mode. Reverted the prompt to use clear keys (`status`, `match`, `case_id`) and implemented robust regex parsing `re.search(r'\\{.*\\}', ...)` to extract JSON from markdown/chatter.\n- **Multithreading**: Implemented `concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6)` in `coordinator.py` to execute LLM batches in parallel, significantly reducing the bottleneck of sequential HTTP requests.\n- **Verification**: The OpenRouter pipeline ran successfully to completion (Matched: 8, Not Found: 542, Needs Review: 41), proving the parsing and API integration work perfectly. The only remaining issue is raw speed.\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n### Architecture & Failures:\n- **Failure - Open Source Model Batch Limits**: Generic 8B models on OpenRouter completely fail to follow instructions if the batch size is too large (e.g., 300 items per prompt). They lose context and return 0 matches. **Constraint**: Batch size for generic models must be kept at ~50.\n- **Failure - $O(N \\times M)$ LLM Bottleneck**: Asking an LLM to read a 200+ item warehouse catalog for every batch of 50 shortage items is computationally heavy and causes massive TTFT (Time to First Token) delays. Even with multithreading, it is too slow for a real-time web app.\n- **Architectural Solution (Hybrid Engine)**: To achieve sub-minute execution, we must use a local lexical/semantic search (e.g., `scikit-learn` TF-IDF Cosine Similarity or `rapidfuzz` top-K extraction). This local step compares the shortage drug against the warehouse and fetches only the Top-3 or Top-5 candidates in milliseconds. The LLM is then only given those 5 candidates to make a final binary judgment, cutting prompt size by 95% and bypassing LLM reasoning bottlenecks.\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files (in `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\`):\n- `src\\config.py`: \n  - **What & Why**: Removed Gemini/OpenCode settings. Added `openrouter_api_key` and set `openrouter_model` to `\"openrouter/free\"`.\n- `src\\match\\coordinator.py`: \n  - **What & Why**: Completely rewritten to drop Google SDK and use `requests.post` to `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions`.\n  - Added parallel batch execution using `ThreadPoolExecutor`.\n  - Reverted the `SYSTEM_PROMPT` to use human-readable JSON schema for open-source model compatibility.\n  - Added regex extraction to safely parse dirty JSON outputs.\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Immediate Context**: The user just ran the multithreaded OpenRouter script to completion. While it works and returns matches, it is still too slow. The user agreed to build the much faster \"Hybrid Engine\" (Local Search + LLM).\n\n**What the