{"step_index":245,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T19:50:05Z","thinking":"**Drafting Coordinator Logic**\n\nOkay, I'm now crafting the `src/fast_match/coordinator.py` file. I'm focusing on the coordinator's key responsibilities: deduplicating shortages and integrating the `FastCandidateFinder`. I'm breaking down the task into distinct steps. I'm focusing on applying the finder to each warehouse, and then determining `top_k=5` candidates per shortage. Additionally, I need to check scores, either above 0.95 or exact string matches.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import json\nimport time\nimport re\nimport concurrent.futures\nimport requests as http_requests\n\nfrom ..config import Config\nfrom .search import FastCandidateFinder\nfrom ..match.text_match import normalize_text\n\n\nSYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a pharmaceutical matching assistant.\nYou will receive a list of cases. Each case has a requested drug name and a list of specific candidate items found in the warehouse.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this exact schema:\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"case_id\": \"string\",\n      \"status\": \"match or no_match or review\",\n      \"item_id\": \"string\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n1. \"match\" means the exact same product, strength, dosage form, and pack size. Set \"item_id\" to the ID of the matching candidate.\n2. \"no_match\" means NONE of the provided candidates are a safe match. Set \"item_id\" to \"\".\n3. \"review\" means there is a plausible candidate but details are ambiguous. Set \"item_id\" to that candidate's ID.\n4. ONLY return results for the cases provided.\n5. DO NOT return markdown blocks. Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass FastCoordinator:\n    def __init__(self, config: Config):\n        self.config = config\n        self.openrouter_api_key = getattr(config, 'openrouter_api_key', None)\n\n    def process(self, shortage_items: list[dict], warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> dict:\n        unique_shortages = {}\n        for item in shortage_items:\n            name = item.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")\n            if name and name not in unique_shortages:\n                unique_shortages[name] = item\n                \n        deduped_shortages = list(unique_shortages.values())\n\n        print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n        print(f\"[FAST ENGINE] Starting Match: {len(shortage_items)} raw -> {len(deduped_shortages)} UNIQUE shortages x {len(warehouse_data)} warehouses\")\n        print(f\"{'='*60}\\n\")\n\n        all_warehouse_results = {}\n        found_in = {}\n\n        for wh_name, wh_items in warehouse_data.items():\n            print(f\"\\n{'-'*40}\")\n            print(f\"[Warehouse] {wh_name} ({len(wh_items)} items)\")\n            print(f\"{'-'*40}\")\n\n            wh_result = self._match_warehouse(deduped_shortages, wh_items, wh_name)\n            all_warehouse_results[wh_name] = wh_result\n\n            for match in wh_result[\"matched\"]:\n                name = match[\"shortage_item\"]\n                found_in.setdefault(name, []).append(wh_name)\n\n        all_shortage_names = {item[\"item_name_raw\"] for item in deduped_shortages}\n        found_names = set(found_in.keys())\n        \n        review_only_names = set()\n        for wh_result in all_warehouse_results.values():\n            for rev in wh_result[\"needs_review\"]:\n                review_only_names.add(rev[\"shortage_item\"])\n\n        not_found_names = all_shortage_names - found_names - review_only_names\n        not_found_items = [\n            {\"name\": name, \"source\": next(\n                (item.get(\"source_file\", \"\") for item in deduped_shortages\n                 if item.get(\"item_name_raw\") == name), \"\"\n            )}\n            for name in sorted(not_found_names)\n        ]\n\n        summary = {\n            \"total_shortages\": len(shortage_items),\n            \"unique_shortages\": len(deduped_shortages),\n            \"matched_count\": len(found_names),\n            \"not_found_count\": len(not_found_names),\n            \"review_count\": len(review_only_names - found_names),\n        }\n\n        return {\n            \"warehouse_results\": all_warehouse_results,\n            \"not_found\": not_found_items,\n            \"summary\": summary,\n        }\n\n    def _match_warehouse(self, shortage_items: list[dict], warehouse_items: list[dict], warehouse_name: str) -> dict:\n        matched = []\n        needs_review = []\n        \n        # 1. Prepare fast search index\n        print(\"  -> Indexing warehouse for Fast Search...\")\n        finder = FastCandidateFinder()\n        wh_catalog = [{\"id\": f\"W-{i:05}\", \"name\": item.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")} for i, item in enumerate(warehouse_items)]\n        finder.fit(wh_catalog)\n        \n        catalog_by_id = {item[\"id\"]: item[\"name\"] for item in wh_catalog}\n        wh_normalized = {normalize_text(name): name for name in [i[\"name\"] for i in wh_catalog]}\n\n        # 2. Filter cases: exact match vs LLM required\n        exact_count = 0\n        llm_cases = []\n        \n        for idx, item in enumerate(shortage_items):\n            shortage_name = item.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")\n            norm_name = normalize_text(shortage_name)\n            \n            if norm_name in wh_normalized:\n                matched.append({\n                    \"shortage_item\": shortage_name,\n                    \"warehouse_item\": wh_normalized[norm_name],\n                    \"confidence\": \"exact\",\n                    \"method\": \"exact_text\"\n                })\n                exact_count += 1\n            else:\n                # Get top 5 candidates locally in milliseconds\n                top_candidates = finder.search(shortage_name, top_k=5)\n                # Format for LLM\n                candidates_for_llm = [{\"id\": c[\"id\"], \"name\": c[\"name\"]} for c in top_candidates]\n                \n                llm_cases.append({\n                    \"case_id\": f\"Q{idx:05}\",\n                    \"requested_name\": shortage_name,\n                    \"candidates\": candidates_for_llm\n                })\n\n        print(f\"  -> Exact Matches: {exact_count}\")\n        \n        # 3. Batch process via LLM for the ambiguous ones\n        if llm_cases and self.openrouter_api_key:\n            print(f\"  -> Sending {len(llm_cases)} ambiguous items to LLM in batches...\")\n            batch_size = 30\n            batches = []\n            for i in range(0, len(llm_cases), batch_size):\n                batches.append((i//batch_size, llm_cases[i:i+batch_size]))\n                \n            def process_batch(batch_data):\n                batch_idx, batch_cases = batch_data\n                max_retries = 3\n                for attempt in range(max_retries):\n                    try:\n                        results = self._call_openrouter({\"cases\": batch_cases})\n                        parsed = []\n                        for case, decision in zip(batch_cases, results):\n                            shortage_name = case[\"requested_name\"]\n                            status = decision.get(\"status\", \"no_match\")\n                            item_id = decision.get(\"item_id\", \"\")\n                            warehouse_item = catalog_by_id.get(item_id, \"\")\n                            \n                            parsed.append({\n                                \"shortage_name\": shortage_name,\n                                \"status\": status,\n                                \"warehouse_item\": warehouse_item\n                            })\n                        print(f\"      [✓] Batch {batch_idx+1}/{len(batches)} done.\")\n                        return parsed\n                    except Exception as e:\n                        if attempt < max_retries - 1:\n                            time.sleep(3)\n                        else:\n                            print(f\"      [!] Batch {batch_idx+1} failed: {e}\")\n                \n                return [{\"shortage_name\": c[\"requested_name\"], \"status\": \"no_match\", \"warehouse_item\": \"\"} for c in batch_cases]\n\n            with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=5) as executor:\n                results_lists = list(executor.map(process_batch, batches))\n                \n            for res_list in results_lists:\n                for result in res_list:\n                    if result[\"status\"] == \"match\":\n                        matched.append({\n                            \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                            \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"],\n                            \"confidence\": \"llm\",\n                            \"method\": \"fast_llm\"\n                        })\n                    elif result[\"status\"] == \"review\":\n                        needs_review.append({\n                            \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                            \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"]\n                        })\n\n        print(f\"  -> Final Warehouse Result: {len(matched)} matched, {len(needs_review)} review\")\n        return {\"matched\": matched, \"needs_review\": needs_review}\n\n    def _call_openrouter(self, inputs: dict) -> list[dict]:\n        model = getattr(self.config, 'openrouter_model', 'openrouter/free')\n        \n        body = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": json.dumps(inputs, ensure_ascii=False)}\n            ]\n        }\n\n        url = \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions\"\n        response = http_requests.post(\n            url,\n            headers={\n                \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {self.openrouter_api_key}\",\n                \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n                \"HTTP-Referer\": \"https://localhost\",\n                \"X-Title\": \"PharmacyMatcher\",\n            },\n            json=body,\n            timeout=(30, 150),\n        )\n\n        if response.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {response.status_code}\")\n\n        content = response.json()[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"]\n        json_match = re.search(r'\\{.*\\}', content, re.DOTALL)\n        if json_match:\n            content = json_match.group(0)\n            \n        answer = json.loads(content)\n        results = answer.get(\"results\", [])\n        \n        # Map by case_id\n        decision_map = {d.get(\"case_id\"): d for d in results}\n        \n        return [decision_map.get(c[\"case_id\"], {\"status\": \"no_match\", \"item_id\": \"\"}) for c in inputs[\"cases\"]]","Description":"Fast coordinator using TF-IDF local filtering and minimal LLM batching","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","toolAction":"Create the fast match coordinator","toolSummary":"Create fast coordinator"}}]}
